invariant: INV-16
file: chacha20_vector.c
catches: chacha20_equiv_test
reason: each group XORs the rows of three of its four lanes, so the
  fourth block of every group keeps the input's bytes: in place, 64 bytes
  of each 256 go out as plaintext. bin/chacha20_equiv_test compares every
  byte of the output with chacha20.c's, at every length that holds a
  whole group.

